**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`

**How to implement.** Each experiment's data status as one pure Domain badge (001 §K 'Status badges: no data / mapped / validated (points) / excluded points / data changed / out of range'; 001 §E 'A changed or missing data file is flagged'; AGENTS.md: behaviour lives in Domain, the view projects it). The window's `ExperimentFileStatus` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:ExperimentFileStatus`) is that status today, so it MOVES into Domain as the badge and is deleted, one type remaining (AGENTS.md 'A bijection is collapsed'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`, after `loadAndValidate`: `ExperimentDataBadge` = `NoDataBadge` (no data) | `MappedDataBadge of problemOpt : ExperimentDataError option` (mapped: a mapped attachment whose points are not validated, with the reason when the file did not read) | `ValidatedDataBadge of points : MeasuredPointCount` (validated, with its points) | `DataChangedBadge of attachment : DataAttachment * currentOpt : ContentHash option` (data changed since attach: the file's hash now, or `None` when it is missing) | `OutOfRangeBadge of problem : ExperimentDataError` (out of range: a range or units mismatch). `member this.text : string` answers `no data`, `mapped`, `validated (<n> points)`, `data changed` and `out of range`. `static member ofCheck (dataOpt : MappedAttachment option) (statusOpt : DataAttachmentStatus option) (outcomeOpt : Result<MeasuredSeries, ExperimentDataError> option) : ExperimentDataBadge` is the one rule: no data is `NoDataBadge`; a status `AttachedDataChanged current` or `AttachedDataMissing` (step 132) is `DataChangedBadge` of the attachment and `Some current` or `None`; an `Ok series` is `ValidatedDataBadge series.pointCount` (`MeasuredData.fs:pointCount`); an `Error` of `DataRangeMismatchErr` or `DataUnitsMismatchErr` is `OutOfRangeBadge`; any other `Error` is `MappedDataBadge (Some e)`; and no outcome is `MappedDataBadge None`. 001's excluded-points badge needs the experiment's exclusions, which S9.3 adds (its `ExcludePoint`), so it arrives with them. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ExperimentFileStatus` and `ExperimentDataError.fileStatus` are deleted; `experimentDataStatus` (step 136) holds an `ExperimentDataBadge` per experiment; the one private validation function (steps 136, 152, 187) and the `AttachDataFileTo` arm compute it by `ofCheck` from the experiment's `dataOpt`, the `attachmentStatus` read (a `KitError` of that read being `MalformedDataFileErr` of its `describe`, as `ExperimentDataStore` maps one, step 135) and the `loadAndValidate` result; an attach the kit refuses keeps the experiment's data and badge and sets `kitStatus` to `Not attached — <e.describe>`. `model.dataBadgeOf (experiment : Experiments.Experiment) : ExperimentDataBadge` is the map's badge, else `ofCheck experiment.dataOpt None None`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type ExperimentDataBadge with member this.caption : ControlCaption` keeps every caption the window showed: `No data`, `Mapped — not validated`, `Parse error — <e.caption>` for a reason, `Loaded — <n> point(s), schema-valid`, `Data changed since attach — attach it again to validate it`, `Data file missing — <path>` and `Validation error — <e.caption>`; `dataFileRow` shows it. Tests. `ExperimentDataProxyTests` gains `the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation`: `ofCheck` of no data is `NoDataBadge` whatever else is given; of a mapped attachment with a changed status `DataChangedBadge` naming the new hash, with a missing one `DataChangedBadge` with `None`, ahead of any outcome; with an `Ok` of the canned intensity series `ValidatedDataBadge` of its `pointCount`; with `DataRangeMismatchErr` and with `DataUnitsMismatchErr` `OutOfRangeBadge`; with `MalformedDataFileErr` `MappedDataBadge (Some _)`; with nothing `MappedDataBadge None`; and the five texts. `InverseConstructorTests` (steps 135, 136, 152): `attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment`, `attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status`, `attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status` and `opening a kit flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing` assert `ValidatedDataBadge`, `MappedDataBadge (Some _)`, `OutOfRangeBadge` and `DataChangedBadge` where they asserted the status cases, their captions unchanged; `a picked file the kit cannot attach records a typed attach-failed status and no attachment` is renamed `a picked file the kit cannot attach records no attachment and tells the kit status why`: the experiment's `dataOpt` stays `None`, its badge `NoDataBadge`, and `kitStatus` holds the reason. `ScrollExtentTests` passes as written.

**Acceptance.** After the data badges land, `ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck` MUST be the one rule giving no data / mapped / validated (points) / data changed / out of range from an experiment's mapped attachment, its file's status and its validation, `ExperimentFileStatus` MUST be gone with every caption kept, and an attach the kit refuses MUST be told in the kit status; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including the renamed `a picked file the kit cannot attach records no attachment and tells the kit status why` and the changed `attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment`, `attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status`, `attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status` and `opening a kit flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing`, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.
